      }
    },
    {
      "understanding": 1,
      "teacher_description": "Describes the path a clip took, or says the data mattered without naming which clips.",
      "ai_prompt": "",
      "seeding_key": {
        "understanding": 1,
        "learning_goal.key": "defdbfc9-1774-4d2d-8727-67359c079ad2",
        "lesson.key": "lesson-8",
        "lesson_group.key": "lessonGroup-2",
        "script.name": "6-12-aid-data-makes-ai-2026"
      }
    },
    {
      "understanding": 2,
      "teacher_description": "Names a specific prediction and the training clips that caused it, and says what change would give a different result. Either the dance clip or the premiere clip works.",
      "ai_prompt": "",
      "seeding_key": {
        "understanding": 2,
        "learning_goal.key": "defdbfc9-1774-4d2d-8727-67359c079ad2",
        "lesson.key": "lesson-8",
        "lesson_group.key": "lessonGroup-2",
        "script.name": "6-12-aid-data-makes-ai-2026"
      }
    },
    {
      "understanding": 3,
      "teacher_description": "Sees a pattern across clips and what it says about how the data was collected.",
      "ai_prompt": "",
      "seeding_key": {
        "understanding": 3,
        "learning_goal.key": "defdbfc9-1774-4d2d-8727-67359c079ad2",
        "lesson.key": "lesson-8",
        "lesson_group.key": "lessonGroup-2",
        "script.name": "6-12-aid-data-makes-ai-2026"
      }
    },
    {
      "understanding": 0,
      "teacher_description": "Says the chat is \"AI\" or \"both\" with no example. Can't tie what happened to a message to any rule.",
      "ai_prompt": "Gives the output with no steps: “it just does it,” “the AI learned it,” or a restated card description. Or traces with a check the system doesn’t actually make. Or skips straight from input to output.\n\nSounds like: “It turns the heat on because it’s cold.” “The spam filter learned what spam is.”",
      "seeding_key": {
        "understanding": 0,
        "learning_goal.key": "f65e0fe2-aed0-4594-8a5a-7af8c343762c",
        "lesson.key": "lesson-3",
        "lesson_group.key": "lessonGroup-2",
        "script.name": "6-12-aid-data-makes-ai-2026"
      }
    },
    {
      "understanding": 1,
      "teacher_description": "Names one human-written rule and one computer-learned rule from the gaming chat, and ties each to what happened to a message.",
      "ai_prompt": "Picks a specific input and names each check the system makes, in order, with the input’s result at each check, ending at the output. For data-trained cards, uses the rules on the peek-inside card. Sounds like: “The room was 65. The thermostat checked whether it’s below 68. It is, so the heat turned on.” / “The email said ‘FREE prize.’ The filter checked for ‘free.’ It had it, so it checked for a link. It had one, so it went to junk.”",
      "seeding_key": {
        "understanding": 1,
        "learning_goal.key": "f65e0fe2-aed0-4594-8a5a-7af8c343762c",
        "lesson.key": "lesson-3",
        "lesson_group.key": "lessonGroup-2",
        "script.name": "6-12-aid-data-makes-ai-2026"
      }
    },
    {
      "understanding": 2,
      "teacher_description": "Also explains why each rule is that kind: exact rules can't judge what a message means, so people gave that job to a rule learned from examples. Says what would have to change to get a different result.",
      "ai_prompt": "Explains where a check came from (a person who wrote it, or examples it was trained on), or what would have to change to get a different output. Sounds like: “A person picked 68. If they’d set it to 65, the heat would stay off.” / “It checks for ‘free’ because lots of the spam it learned from said ‘free.’ Without that word, my email would go to the inbox.”",
      "seeding_key": {
        "understanding": 2,
        "learning_goal.key": "f65e0fe2-aed0-4594-8a5a-7af8c343762c",
        "lesson.key": "lesson-3",
        "lesson_group.key": "lessonGroup-2",
        "script.name": "6-12-aid-data-makes-ai-2026"
      }
    },
    {
      "understanding": 3,
      "teacher_description": "Rare here. Sees a pattern across many messages and reasons about what the learned rule must have been trained on.",
      "ai_prompt": "Recognizes that a check will repeat across a whole group of inputs. Or, for a data-trained card with no peek-inside card, works out a likely rule by comparing several outputs. Sounds like: “It’s not just my email. Every real message that says ‘free’ will end up in junk.”",
      "seeding_key": {
        "understanding": 3,
        "learning_goal.key": "f65e0fe2-aed0-4594-8a5a-7af8c343762c",
        "lesson.key": "lesson-3",
        "lesson_group.key": "lessonGroup-2",
        "script.name": "6-12-aid-data-makes-ai-2026"
      }
    },
